 ## Subtopics
 
-### Cube Assisted Raymarching
-A variant that stores the size of the largest possible cube around each empty cell instead of a sphere [S2, unofficial]. It is faster to compute (order of magnitude faster) but slightly suboptimal for step size compared to sphere-assisted [S2, unofficial]. It uses a summed area table (SAT) to compute the area of arbitrary boxes in $O(1)$ time, allowing binary search for the maximum cube size in $O(\log n)$ per voxel, reducing upfront complexity from $O(n^2)$ to $O(n \log n)$ [S2, unofficial].
+### [Cube Assisted Raymarching](4940-cube-assisted-raymarching.md)
+A variant that stores the size of the largest possible cube around each empty cell instead of a sphere. It is faster to compute (order of magnitude faster) but slightly suboptimal for step size compared to sphere-assisted. It uses a summed area table (SAT) to compute the area of arbitrary boxes in $O(1)$ time, allowing binary search for the maximum cube size in $O(\log n)$ per voxel, reducing upfront complexity from $O(n^2)$ to $O(n \log n)$.
 
